{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1559190-advice-for-swift-spirit-of-winged-transportation-as-a-control-spell","id":1559190,"title":"Advice For Swift Spirit of Winged Transportation as a Control Spell","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-02T17:17:07-07:00","id":1559190,"title":"Advice For Swift Spirit of Winged Transportation as a Control Spell","content":"Adapting Swift Spirit of Winged Transportation to 3e is mostly trivial, except I'm uncertain what effects it should have as a control spell. One thought I had is: &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Sorcerers who have this as their control spell can ask the spirit to remain nearby for up to one full day after the end of a journey, and if they ask the spirit to perform another journey, they need not cast the spell a second time. In addition, they can ride on the spirit, or even ask it to carry on its back a large carriage capable of holding 10 people, and several hundred pounds of cargo, with space just outside the carriage sufficient to hold up to two animals the size of Simhata. While riding the spirit in this fashion, the sorcerer can also ask the spirit to pick up, carry, or drop buildings, ships, vast boulders, and similar objects, just as it normally can.</span>&quot; <br /> <br /> However, I'm not certain this is quite right. What are your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}